    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0663" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg449"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 210.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Fish to General
                        Schenck</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            20, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to my No. 3 of the 19th ultimo,
                    in relation to the pending negotiations of a consular convention with the
                    British government, I will thank you to propose the adoption of an article
                    providing for the administration of oaths by the consuls of either country
                    residing in the other. This you will do at such time and in such manner as may,
                    in your judgment, be most opportune and appropriate. This is especially to be
                    desired by this Government, as consuls are required, by existing Treasury
                    regulations, to see that all invoices verified by them are supported by the oath
                    of the party.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
